<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Schönborn family</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as House of Schönborn</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Schönborn are a German noble family from the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rhineland">Rhineland</a> who rose to great power in the church in the 17th and 18th centuries. Members of the family were <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/prince-elector">electors</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mainz">Mainz</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/trier">Trier</a> and prince-<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bishop">bishops</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/wurzburg">Würzburg</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bamberg">Bamberg</a>, Speyer and Constance. They were great builders, commissioning baroque palaces such as the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/wurzburg-residence">Würzburg Residence</a>, Pommersfelden and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bruchsal">Bruchsal</a> from architects including <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/balthasar-neumann">Balthasar Neumann</a>.</p></div>
